body:
## Motivation (paper-driven)

["The Red Queen Gödel Machine: Co-Evolving Agents and Their Evaluators" (arXiv:2606.26294)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26294) argues that in self-improving agent systems, **evaluation must be part of the improvement loop** — static, out-of-loop gates get stale or gamed. Its headline empirical result is that adding a *cheap* code reviewer to the improvement loop beat the prior state of the art (HGM-H) on Polyglot with 1.35–1.72× fewer search tokens: a reviewer is the cheapest high-leverage addition to a self-modification pipeline.

["Latent Programming Horizons in Coding Agents" (arXiv:2607.05188)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.05188) (KTH) shows that coding-agent LMs internally track whether the evolving program parses, passes tests, and introduces regressions — *ahead of their own edits*. Practical corollary: mechanical verification signals (tests, lint) align with what the model already represents; a pipeline that doesn't surface or enforce them wastes the strongest available signal.

waffle's self-development loop is architecturally in great shape (sandboxed self-workspace, git audit trail, doctor-gated atomic swap, rollback) — but the *gate* is thinner than `docs/plan.md` promises.

## Current behaviour

- `selfdev.Upgrade` (`internal/selfdev/selfdev.go:101`) runs `go build`, then the **new binary's** `doctor`, then swaps. That's it.
- `docs/plan.md:229-231` says a self-change "must get `go build`, `go vet`, `go test -race`, and `golangci-lint` green *inside the workspace*" — but nothing mechanical enforces this anywhere. The workspace stage trusts the agent to have run them; the deploy stage doesn't re-check. A self-change with a failing test suite deploys cleanly today if it compiles and doctor passes (doctor checks config/DB/secrets, not correctness).
- `docs/plan.md:232-235`'s approval gate ("review every diff / review PRs with CI green / auto-land patch-level changes … config-per-instance") has **no config key and no code**.
- There is no review stage of any kind between "agent edited code" and "binary swapped in".

## Proposed change

### 1. Verify stage in `Upgrade` (mechanical gate)

```go
// verify runs the plan-mandated checks in repoDir. golangci-lint is optional
// tooling: missing binary is a warning, a failing run is a failure.
func verify(ctx context.Context, repoDir string, stderr io.Writer) error {
    steps := [][]string{
        {"go", "vet", "./..."},
        {"go", "test", "-race", "./..."},
    }
    if _, err := exec.LookPath("golangci-lint"); err == nil {
        steps = append(steps, []string{"golangci-lint", "run"})
    } else {
        fmt.Fprintln(stderr, "warning: golangci-lint not installed; lint gate skipped")
    }
    for _, s := range steps {
        if err := run(ctx, repoDir, stderr, s[0], s[1:]...); err != nil {
            return fmt.Errorf("verify: %s failed: %w", strings.Join(s, " "), err)
        }
    }
    return nil
}
```

Called between checkout and build in `Upgrade`; skippable only via an explicit `waffle upgrade --no-verify` documented as unsafe.

### 2. Approval policy in config

```toml
[selfdev]
approval = "manual"    # "manual" | "ci" | "auto-patch"
verify   = true
# paths a change may never auto-land into, regardless of approval mode
protected = ["internal/secret", "internal/gateway"]
```

### 3. Reviewer stage (the Red Queen result, operationalized)

Before a self-PR is pushed for landing, run a structured review of the diff with the cheap/utility model (see #61):

```go
// Reviewer critiques a self-change before it is proposed for landing.
type Reviewer struct {
    Provider llm.Provider
    Model    string // utility model — the paper's reviewer is deliberately cheap
}

type Finding struct {
    Severity string // "blocker" | "warn" | "nit"
    File     string
    Summary  string
}

// Review returns findings for the diff given the task that motivated it.
// Blockers stop the land; everything is persisted to the session transcript
// so git + transcript together form the audit trail.
func (r *Reviewer) Review(ctx context.Context, diff, task string) ([]Finding, error)
```

The prompt asks specifically: does the diff match the stated task, does it touch protected paths, does it weaken any gate (tests deleted/skipped, doctor checks removed, verify bypassed)? That last check matters: **a self-modifying system's evaluator must itself be protected from the modifications it evaluates** — which is the Red Queen paper's core warning.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `waffle upgrade` refuses to swap when `go vet`, `go test -race`, or (if installed) `golangci-lint` fail; the failing step's output is shown; test proves a repo with one failing test never swaps the binary.
- [ ] `--no-verify` exists, is off by default, and is flagged as unsafe in `--help` and docs.
- [ ] Missing `golangci-lint` binary degrades to a warning (and `waffle doctor` gains a check reporting whether the lint gate is armed).
- [ ] `[selfdev] approval` is parsed, defaults to `manual`, and unknown values are rejected at config load (consistent with waffle's reject-unknown-keys stance).
- [ ] `auto-patch` mode refuses any diff touching `protected` paths, and refuses any diff that modifies the verify/reviewer/doctor code paths themselves.
- [ ] Reviewer stage produces structured findings; `blocker` findings stop the land in `manual` and `auto-patch` modes; findings are persisted (transcript or SQLite) with the commit SHA they reviewed.
- [ ] Reviewer uses the utility model when configured (#61) so review cost stays a fraction of generation cost.
- [ ] `docs/plan.md` self-development section updated to describe the implemented gate instead of the aspirational one.

## Interactions

- #21 fixed ref validation in this same code path; this issue completes the hardening at the semantic level.
- The evaluation-harness issue (filed alongside) plugs its deterministic eval tier into this verify stage.

*Raised from a literature review against arXiv:2606.26294 ([abs](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26294)) and arXiv:2607.05188 ([abs](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.05188)).*
